# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your deployed API base URL.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables are embedded in the app bundle in plain text,
# so put ONLY non-secret values here (an endpoint URL is fine; API keys are NOT).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://YOUR_API_ID.execute-api.ap-northeast-1.amazonaws.com/Prod

# ⚠️ The API key does NOT go here - there is deliberately no variable for it.
# It is typed into the app's settings screen and kept in expo-secure-store
# (src/api/apiKey.ts). Retrieve the value with the command in Backend/README.md.

# --- Release signing (upload key), only needed to build for Google Play -----
# Required by `npm run bundle:play`, which produces the AAB uploaded to the
# Play internal testing track (adr/009). A plain `expo run:android` does NOT
# need these: without them the release build falls back to the debug key,
# which Play will not accept.
#
# ⚠️ These are SECRETS. `.env` is gitignored - keep it that way, and never
# commit the keystore itself. The keystore lives OUTSIDE this repository
# (~/.keystore/), so that deleting the repo cannot take the key with it.
#
# ⚠️ Losing the upload key is recoverable: with Play App Signing you can
# request an upload key reset in the Play Console (24-48h). The key that is
# NOT recoverable is the app signing key, which Google holds for you.
#
# Setup instructions (how to generate the keystore) are in SETUP.md.
# ⚠️ Quote the passwords. This file is read with the shell's `source`, so an
# unquoted `#` truncates the value and an unquoted space is parsed as a command
# - either way the variable ends up empty and signing fails with a confusing error.
# TRG_KEYSTORE_PATH=/Users/you/.keystore/touring-upload.jks
# TRG_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=''
# TRG_KEY_ALIAS=upload
# TRG_KEY_PASSWORD=''
